 Price\\* | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK Apartment  600 Sq. Ft. | **Price on Request** | Check Availability |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  1600 Sq. Ft. | **Price on Request** | Check Availability |\n\n\\*Prices are indicative and subject to applicable charges and project terms.\n\n### Price Trends\n\nRaheja Green's average asking price is stable quarter-on-quarter, compared with Borivali East.\n\nSep 2025 — Jun 2026\n\n| Quarter | Raheja Green | Borivali East |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Jun 2026 | 30100 | 35200 |\n| Mar 2026 | 30300 | 34750 |\n| Dec 2025 | 28950 | 32450 |\n| Sep 2025 | 29650 | 30650 |\n\n### Comparable Projects\n\nRaheja Green avg. price is ₹ 30.1 K/Sq.Ft. compared to Borivali East at ₹ 35.2 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Project | Avg. ₹/sq ft |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Hiranandani Heritage Pristina](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/hiranandani-heritage-pristina/27925/project \"Hiranandani Heritage Pristina\") | ₹ 36,750 |\n| Borivali East | ₹ 35,200 |\n| [Rustomjee Regency](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/rustomjee-regency/3692/project \"Rustomjee Regency\") | ₹ 31,150 |\n| [Kolte Patil Vaayu](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/kolte-patil-vaayu/105334/project \"Kolte Patil Vaayu\") | ₹ 31,000 |\n| Current Project **Raheja Green** | ₹ 30,100 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Borivali East ranges from ₹ 19.1 K to ₹ 1.5 L with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3,4 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In Raheja Green | In Borivali East |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 31.8 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 46.2 K |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 98.6 K |\n| 4 BHK | - | ₹ 1.5 L |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for Raheja Green.\n\n#### MMRDA Plans Two New Ring Roads to Ease Mumbai Traffic\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) is planning two additional ring routes, expanding its proposed network from seven to nine. These new corridors will cover approximately 307 km and will connect existing roads and planned projects across Mumbai, Thane, and Navi Mumbai.\n\n#### Thane Infrastructure and Development Updates\n\nThe Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel project saw the launch of TBM Arjuna on August 13, 2026, aiming to reduce travel time between Thane and Borivali to approximately 15 minutes. Amazon Data Services is developing a large data center in Ambernath, with an estimated construction cost of ₹3,500 crore, to be ready by 2029\n\n#### Mumbai Boosts Connectivity with Santacruz - Chembur link road Phase 2 & Chembur Metro Station\n\nCM Devendra Fadnavis inaugurated Phase 2 of the Santacruz-Chembur Link Road (SCLR) & the Chembur Metro Station under Metro Line 2B,The SCLR Phase 2 is expected to strengthen the road network between Mumbai's western and eastern suburbs, improving east-west connectivity.\n\n#### Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel Project: Traffic Diversions Announced in Kasarvadavali\n\nTemporary traffic diversions have been implemented in Kasarvadavali for the ongoing work on the ambitious Thane-Borivali twin tunnel project by the Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA). Certain routes will be closed from July 6 to August 5, 2026, to facilitate construction.\n\n#### Mumbai Monorail Services to Resume After Nine-Month Hiatus\n\nMumbai's monorail services are set to resume soon after a nine-month suspension, following approval from the Maharashtra government for safety improvements and fare revisions. MMRDA has proposed increased ticket prices. The monorail, which previously carried around 18,000 passengers daily, will offer improved services after safety upgrades.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\n#### MMRDA to Launch Metro Lines 2B and 9, Bhoomipujan for Thane-Borivali Tunnel and BKC Pod Taxi on April 7\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) will inaugurate Metro Line 2B (Phase I) and Metro Line 9 (Phase I), and conduct the bhoomipujan for the Thane–Borivali Twin Tunnel project and the pod taxi system in Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC) on April 7. These projects aim to significantly reduce travel time, ease congestion, and improve connectivity across Mumbai's suburbs.\n\n### Govt. Registrations\n\n1 Sales Transactions Registered in Raheja Green From Oct 25 to Sep 26 at Avg. Price ₹ 22.6 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Sales Transactions | Gross Sales Value | Registered Rate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | - | ₹ 22,600 / Sq. Ft. |\n\nTransaction Period Oct 25 to Sep 26\n\n## Raheja Green Floor Plans\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 1 BHK 600 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Raheja Green, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:Price on Request\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 3 BHK 1600 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Raheja Green, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:Price on Request\n\n## Amenities & Specifications of Raheja Green\n\n### Sports Sports\n\n![Sports](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/sports/am-ico-kidsplay-active.svg)\n\n### Convenience Convenience\n\n![Convenience](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/convenience/am-ico-powerbac-active.svg)\n\n### Safety Safety\n\n![Safety](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/safety/am-ico-24x7secu-active.svg)\n\n### Environment Environment\n\n![Environment](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/environment/am-ico-normalpa-active.svg)\n\n### Specifications\n\n## Location and Connectivity Around Raheja Universal Borivali East\n\n![Connectivity map showing nearby places around Mumbai Western Suburbs](/assets/images/project-map.png?aio=w-714;h-317;crop;)\n\nEstimate commute from your office or kid's school to Raheja Green.\n\n![Car travel mode](/assets/images/car-fill.svg)\n![Raheja Green](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/raheja-green-project-project-large-image1.jpg?aio=w-112;h-96;crop;)\n\nPlease select the starting point to calculate the travel time.\n\n![Rolling loader icon](/assets/images/rolling-loader.gif)\n\n### Nearby Landmarks\n\n#### Gopal Garden High School\n\n#### Borivali National Park Bus Stop\n\n#### Arihant Heart And Surgical Hospital\n\nAverage Asking Price in Borivali East\n\nBased on active listings and recent trends\n\nUpcoming metro and monorail networks\n\nHuge increase in population\n\n![Key insight rating icon](/assets/images/key-insights-icon/key-insights-rating